[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Branch-coverage evidence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A row is only checked off once the branch it targets is *proven* to have run.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each solver/dispatcher test classifies its own inputs with the same predicates
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the C uses and fails if any arm was never reached. Measured on the default seed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c22  arms:                 keep-a=13568  keep-b=6555  edge=19877
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c23  arms:                 A=9953 B=2520 C=2717 AB=4657 BC=3643 CA=3507 interior=13003
