[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c2GJK loop exits:          Hit, NoProgress, DegenerateDir, Dup   (IterCap proven unreachable)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c2GJK use_radius arms:     SkippedByHit, Disabled, Shrink, ShrinkCollapsed, Midpoint
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c2GJK cache metric guard:  rejected=1600  accepted=6496  (NaN-metric accepts=534)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m c2GJK cache counts seen:   count1=6306  count2=2477  count3=1297
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reverse_collide results:   all 8 bitmask values 0..7 produced
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    166[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    167[0m:[38;5;10m[49m For `c2GJK`, whose five loop exits and five `use_radius` arms are not visible in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    168[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the return value, the control flow is re-traced in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    169[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/common/mod.rs :: classify()` using the **C library's own exported
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    170[0m:[38;5;10m[49m primitives** (`c2MakeProxy`, `c22`, `c23`, `c2L`, `c2D`, `c2Support`, `c2Witness`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    171[0m:[38;5;10m[49m … all via `dlsym`). That is used only to label an input for coverage
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    172[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bookkeeping; the correctness assertion is always the C-vs-Rust comparison.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    173[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    174[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Comparison policy
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    175[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    176[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Outputs are decomposed into typed 4-byte lanes (`Lane::F` / `Lane::I`) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    177[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compared lane-by-lane; `tests/layout.rs` asserts the decomposition covers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    178[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `size_of::<T>() / 4` words for every struct, so no byte is skipped and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    179[0m:[38;5;10m[49m padding can hide a difference.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    180[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    181[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every value class is compared **bit-for-bit**: ordinary values, `+0` vs `-0`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    182[0m:[38;5;10m[49m denormals, and infinities. The single exception is the **payload and sign of a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    183[0m:[38;5;10m[49m NaN**, which is compared only as "both are NaN". IEEE 754 and the C standard both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    184[0m:[38;5;10m[49m leave NaN payload propagation unspecified, and the two toolchains legitimately
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    185[0m:[38;5;10m[49m differ: `gcc -O0` compiles `a.x += b.x` to `addss %xmm1(a.x),%xmm0(b.x)`, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    186[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *second* operand's NaN survives, while LLVM keeps `a.x` in the destination and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    187[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *first* survives; LLVM also folds `-a.s*b.x + a.c*b.y` into an `fsub`, which does
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    188[0m:[38;5;10m[49m not flip the NaN sign that the C's explicit negation does. No NaN payload is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    189[0m:[38;5;10m[49m observable through any comparison this library performs, so it cannot affect any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    190[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `int` or boolean result. `tests/layout.rs :: comparator_rejects_real_differences`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m proves the tolerance does not leak: a 1-ulp change, a `+0`/`-0` flip and an `int`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m field change are all still rejected.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Restrictions (undefined behaviour in the C, not differentially testable)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    195[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    196[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Row 65** only reuses a cache whose stored indices are in range for the new
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    197[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   proxies. `c2MakeProxy` writes only `verts[0 .. count)`, so an out-of-range
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    198[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   index makes the C read `c2Proxy` slots it never initialised.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    199[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `c2GJK` with a `C2_TYPE` outside `{0,1,2}` is excluded for the same reason,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    200[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and worse: the uninitialised `pA.count` reaches `c2Support` as a loop bound and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    201[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   SIGSEGVs. See the corresponding entry in `ERRORS.md`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    202[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    203[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Reproducing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    204[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    205[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    206[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build \
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    207[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   && cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    208[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cd ../../translation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    209[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cargo build --release          # produces the Rust .so the tests dlopen
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    210[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ./check_symbols.sh             # Phase A / D symbol parity
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    211[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ./check_features.sh            # Phases B-D under every feature combination
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    212[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cargo test                     # the differential suite
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    213[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    214[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # Confirm the results are not an artefact of one seed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    215[0m:[38;5;10m[49m for o in 0 1 2 7 13 101 4242 999983; do DIFF_SEED_OFFSET=$o cargo test; done
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    216[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    217[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    218[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Note: the C `.so` is linked **without `-lm`**, so its `sqrtf` is left undefined.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    219[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The harness `dlopen`s `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_GLOBAL` before loading it
